course: dictionary
lesson: 1998
title: Conceit and showing off
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Conceit is a noun. It means thinking far too well of yourself, being too proud of how clever, good-looking or important you are. The adjective is «conceited», which describes the person who has it.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «He almost danced along the road in his satisfaction and conceit.» He is so pleased with himself that he dances along, so conceit must mean being very proud of yourself. Swap in your meaning: "he danced along, very proud of himself" still makes sense.
explain: Conceited and boastful are close, but not the same. Conceited means thinking too much of yourself. Boastful means always showing off about what you have or do. In The Wind in the Willows, Toad is full of conceit, and the book calls one of his songs «perhaps the most conceited song that any animal ever composed».
fact: Conceit means thinking far too well of yourself.
fact: «Conceited» is the adjective for a person who is full of conceit.
fact: Humility, which means being humble, is the opposite of conceit.
fact: In poetry, a conceit is a clever, surprising comparison or idea.
fact: Badger calls Toad's songs «conceit and boasting», so conceit and boasting are linked but not the same word.
exercise: «He almost danced along the road in his satisfaction and conceit.» What does conceit mean here? | Being lost on the road | Feeling cold and tired | Singing very quietly | *Being very proud of yourself
exercise: Which word is the opposite of conceit? | Boasting | Showing off | *Being humble | Singing loudly
exercise: Which word describes a person who is full of conceit? | Gentle | Shy | *Conceited | Humble
test: Toad sings «conceited songs» in the book. What does conceited tell you about the songs? | Written down in a book | Very sad and slow | Sung in whispers | *Full of too much self-praise
test: Badger says the songs are «conceit and boasting». Which meaning fits best? | Speed and noise | *Too much pride and showing off | Sadness and tiredness | Quiet and gentle kindness
exam: Which sentence shows conceit? | *Ravi kept telling everyone he was the best at everything and never let anyone else speak | Mia thanked everyone for helping and said her friends did most of the work | Jo said sorry and went to bed early | Sam shared his sandwich with the new girl
